{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BX9dfyvPvEZHBgAUB",
	"notes": "A working field Inquisitor — Eisenhorn or Ravenor in their prime, not a centuries-old Lord Inquisitor running whole sub-sectors (that belongs in framework.md's \"Heroes and legends\" tier, well above this template). Point math: ST 11 (+10), DX 14 (+80), IQ 15 (+100), HT 12 (+20) = 210, plus Will +2 (+10) = 220; advantages +40 plus Inquisitorial Rank 6 (+60) and Status 5 (+25); disadvantages -37; skills +255. Total 563 points, upper end of framework.md's \"Senior agents\" tier. Authority comes from three traits together: the Rosette (Legal Enforcement Powers: arrest, search, execute), Inquisitorial Rank (overrides every Imperial hierarchy) and Status (social standing).\nRetinue and means: the template does not price a retinue, Wealth or requisition. An Inquisitor's rosette lets them requisition kit and personnel, so treat retinue members as Allies (built from the Inquisitorial Acolyte and Interrogator templates) and Wealth as campaign purchases, added per character.\nPuritan vs. Radical: this template is written Puritan-neutral. A strict Puritan build should add Intolerance (Xenos) (-10, Imperium/ Traits/Imperial Traits.adq) and lean on the Ordo Hereticus/Malleus lenses; a Radical build (xenotech users, daemonhosts, etc.) should drop or reinterpret Intolerance (Heretics) and is otherwise unrestricted by this template — Radicalism is a stance on methods and sanctioned lore, not a separate stat block, per how Eisenhorn's own arc treats it.\nNo psychic abilities here; many Inquisitors are sanctioned psykers, but that is a separate purchase from the psyker power library, not part of this baseline.\nEnable at most one Ordo lens (all disabled by default); an Inquisitor belongs to exactly one Ordo. They are small flavor packages, not full specialisations — a real Ordo Malleus Inquisitor's daemon-hunting expertise should mostly show up as bought-up Hidden Lore (Daemons) and Hidden Lore (The Warp) levels, not a lens.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tPpi9FJrFAwD7P08t",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Inquisitors survive long enough to reach this rank partly through personal fitness.\n\nDesign: ST 11 (+1), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 10,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tM2sCIdMNzsW9JY49",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A veteran of countless personal confrontations, armed and otherwise.\n\nDesign: DX 14 (+4), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 80,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 4
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t9wz4EVxqxxFz-Gn1",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Eisenhorn and Ravenor are both written as formidably intelligent, solving cases that defeat entire Arbites precincts and Ordo cells.\n\nDesign: IQ 15 (+5), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 100,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": 5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tScJBdHOyfB9nXqly",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Decades of fieldwork, often ending in violence, demand real endurance.\n\nDesign: HT 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 2
